# What the build context may NOT contain. This file is the first line of defence against a
# credential reaching a published image: anything excluded here cannot be COPYed even by
# mistake, and `docker build` does not consult .gitignore.
#
# Everything that .gitignore excludes for the same reason is repeated here on purpose --
# the two files are read by different tools and neither implies the other.

# Runtime state, credentials included: data/ holds config.yaml, the sessions, the API keys,
# the GitHub cache and the traces. It belongs on a mounted volume, never in an image layer --
# baking it in would ship one deployment's credentials and prompts to everybody who pulls the
# image. config.example.yaml (the placeholder template) is deliberately NOT ignored: it is what
# a missing config.yaml is seeded from at startup.
data/
config.yaml
.env
.env.*
logs/
*.log

# Scratch space. Working notes here have held real credentials.
tmp/

# Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Frontend. node_modules/ is reinstalled inside the build stage (a host tree may hold
# native modules built for the wrong platform), and dist/ is rebuilt from source so the
# image can never ship a stale bundle a developer forgot to rebuild.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
node_modules/

# Not needed at runtime, and excluded so editing them cannot invalidate the build cache.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
docs/
verify/
README.md
Dockerfile
.playwright-mcp/

# IDE / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
